The code  group.partial=c("itemX~1")  would relax an equality constraint on an intercept. So this might be someone who established metric or weak invariance, failed to get strong or metric invariance, and now is looking to settle for partial strong invariance. Your code  ("F1 =~ am15")  would relax a constraint on a loading, so you would be giving up on full weak or metric invariance and trying to establish partial weak invariance. That would be the difference.

