> 1) So, in the total effects, should I include all indirect effects including -1 SD, mean, +1 SD? For example, regarding the total effects of X1 on Y,

I think the convention is to report indirect effects at those levels of the moderator. The definition of your indirect effects is also incorrect. They should be:

#indirect effects (x1 -> Z1 -> Y)
x1.indirect. := a1*b1
x1.indirect2 := a1*(b1-1*l)
x1.indirect3 := a1*(b1+1*l)

And these three effects do NOT add up to the total effect. I suggest reviewing David Kenny's webpage (https://davidakenny.net/cm/mediate.htm) to understand the relationship between the total effect and the indirect and direct effects.

> 2) I understand I need to include the direct effects of x1 and x2 on y, though I am not interested in them. But I wonder if those direct effects should be reported in the results section in a paper (e.g., path diagram), though I didn't hypothesize it.

Yes, you should include them in the model and report their estimates.

Best wishes,
Wen Wei

