I forgot to add that some researchers also add (free) the covariance between the residual of mediator (Z1) and the moderator (Z2), i.e., Z2 ~~ Z1, e.g., Model 3 in Preacher, Rucker, and Hayes (2007)

Preacher, K. J., Rucker, D. D., & Hayes, A. F. (2007). Addressing moderated mediation hypotheses: Theory, methods, and prescriptions. Multivariate Behavioral Research, 42(1), 185–227. https://doi.org/10.1080/00273170701341316

As shown in the previous post, this covariance is also fixed to zero by default in lavaan

-- Shu Fai

